## Context

The bibliography quality table (`tab_exp2_bib_quality.tex`, ticket 0264) reveals a
coverage–certainty tradeoff across Exp2 agents and arms: agents that enumerate more
plants tend to cite lower-quality sources, and vice versa.  GPT optimised maximises
both (148 rows, 88% primary); Qwen optimised trades breadth for citation discipline
(15 rows, 55% primary); Claude optimised achieves high coverage (127 rows) at lower
primary rate (28%).

This ticket tracks a scatter plot of that tradeoff across all 40 individual runs
(not just the per-agent means).  The plot is the visual core of the "key tradeoff of
the talk": any system that targets complete provenance necessarily limits its own
coverage, and vice versa.

## Relevant files

- `report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv` — per-run source data (40 rows)
- `src/aedist/extract_exp2_bib.py` — parser that produced the CSV
- `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` — existing three-panel figure (palette reference)
- `report/exp2-analysis.mk` — Makefile target to wire in

## Actions

1. Write `src/aedist/plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py`:
   - X axis: `n_rows` (coverage — inventory table row count)
   - Y axis: `src1_primary / src1_present` (certainty — primary rate among cited rows)
   - One point per run; colour by agent (project palette); shape by arm (filled circle = optimised, open circle = naive)
   - Label outliers: any point where n_rows > 100 or primary_rate > 0.8
   - CLI: `--input` (CSV), `--output` (PDF)
   - Output: `report/inputs/generated/fig_exp2_coverage_certainty.pdf`

2. Wire Makefile target in `report/exp2-analysis.mk`:
   - Prerequisite: `$(GEN)/tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv`
   - Output: `$(GEN)/fig_exp2_coverage_certainty.pdf`
   - Add to `exp2-analysis-report` phony target

3. Add `\input` or `\includegraphics` reference in the appropriate section of
   `slides/manuscript/main.md` (§4, after the provenance-quality paragraph).

## Test

```python
# tests/test_plot_exp2_coverage_certainty.py

def test_script_runs_without_error(tmp_path):
    """End-to-end: script reads CSV and writes a PDF without crashing."""
    import subprocess, sys
    out = tmp_path / "fig.pdf"
    result = subprocess.run(
        [sys.executable, "-m", "aedist.plot_exp2_coverage_certainty",
         "--input", "report/inputs/generated/tab_exp2_bib_quality.csv",
         "--output", str(out)],
        capture_output=True,
    )
    assert result.returncode == 0, result.stderr.decode()
    assert out.exists() and out.stat().st_size > 1000
```

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Scatter PDF generated for all runs with plottable data (non-zero inventory rows and at least one Source 1 citation); excluded runs documented in caption
- [ ] Agent colours match project palette (`palette.toml`)
- [ ] Makefile idempotent (second `make` does not rebuild)
- [ ] `make check-fast` passes
